      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Gas exchange and central hemodynamic parameters were examined in 70 patients with coronary heart disease and 40 healthy subjects during exercise. A low diagnostic informative value of threshold oxygen consumption values was found in the patients with coronary heart disease. It was shown that it was possible to indicate the anaerobic threshold in the patients by analysing the dynamics of cardiac output during exercise."},
